        "settings": {},
        "to_persona": "jupyter-ai-personas::jupyter_ai_acp_client::OpenCodeAcpPersona"
      },
      "body": "[c for c in g.columns if len({str(x) for x in g[c]}) > 1]\n\u89e3\u91ca\u4e00\u4e0b",
      "sender": "58ca9880062344d0831cec3081934d3c"
    },
    {
      "type": "msg",
      "time": 1788403614.061054,
      "body": "This list comprehension finds columns in a DataFrame `g` that have **more than one unique value** (i.e., non-constant columns).\n\n**Breakdown:**\n- `g[c]` - selects column `c` from DataFrame `g`\n- `{str(x) for x in g[c]}` - creates a set of unique string values in that column\n- `len(...) > 1` - checks if there are at least 2 distinct values\n- Returns columns where this condition is true\n\n**Purpose:** Filters out columns where all values are identical, keeping only columns with variation.",
      "mentions": [],
      "sender": "jupyter-ai-personas::jupyter_ai_acp_client::OpenCodeAcpPersona",
      "raw_time": false,
      "id": "ebc82648-3c62-4454-ae61-b01beb8af48d"
    }
  ],
